From e78c9f4991dd239ae87b14129d9f3cd1de86eab1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "T. Kurt Bond" <tkurtbond@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 14:13:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 37/67] Features.md: SET has 32 bits under -OC too

The table of sizes under -O2 and -OC said SET has 64 bits under -OC.
Commit 7f4b284a ("Correct set size in component pascal compatability
mode", 2019) made it 32 bits, as in Component Pascal (OPM.Mod: SetSize
:= 4 for both); SYSTEM.SET64 is the 64-bit set.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 doc/Features.md | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/doc/Features.md b/doc/Features.md
index ffcb4a93..e3ab3bc6 100644
--- a/doc/Features.md
+++ b/doc/Features.md
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@ type implementations.
 | SHORTINT | 8 bit                | 16 bit     |
 | INTEGER  | 16 bit               | 32 bit     |
 | LONGINT  | 32 bit               | 64 bit     |
-| SET      | 32 bit               | 64 bit     |
+| SET      | 32 bit               | 32 bit     |
 
 
 The following Oberon types are independent of compiler size:
-- 
2.55.0

